cloudtak-plugin-sar
This plugin is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 only. See LICENSE.
The plugin imports files of the CloudTAK app (src/std.ts, src/stores/app.ts,
src/base/subscription.ts and a menu template), so the built CloudTAK web bundle that includes it
is a combined work under AGPL-3.0.
The analysis backend is TAK-NZ/sar-engine, a fork of WiSAR Terrain-Aware Range Rings by
Jamie F. Weleber (AGPL-3.0): https://github.com/clptak/WiSAR-Terrain-Aware-Range-Rings
Third-party data and method
The engine returns these attributions, which the plugin shows next to the contours:
  Land cover: LCDB v6.0, Landcare Research, CC BY 4.0
  Elevation: LINZ NZ Elevation, CC BY 4.0, with Copernicus GLO-30
  Roads and trails: OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL, https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
  Method: WiSAR Terrain-Aware Range Rings, AGPL-3.0
TARR mode adds:
  Subject distances: Koester (2008), Lost Person Behavior, via Ferguson (2013), IGT4SAR
  Calibration multipliers: WiSAR, Coconino County, Arizona (not calibrated for New Zealand)
The engine sends these lines with a TARR result too.

Code adapted from other projects
  lib/zip.ts, lib/DataSyncList.vue, lib/DataSyncPicker.vue and lib/missions.ts are adapted from
  TAK-NZ/cloudtak-plugin-rubbersheet (Apache License 2.0): the store-only zip writer, the Data Sync
  list with checkbox rows, and the list of subscribed Data Syncs.
  lib/kml.ts follows the KML export of the WiSAR reference tool (AGPL-3.0), function
  downloadContoursKml in app/static/app.js.
